<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Sun in the Sky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">widely sung by <a href="/years/1949">1949</a>; on record in <a href="/years/1974">1974</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as 天上太阳红彤彤, Tiānshàng tàiyáng hóng tōngtōng</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Red Sun in the Sky&quot; is a Chinese Communist revolutionary song in honour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>. Its words were written by Xu Wenjing and its music by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> Yang, who adapted it from &quot;Ballad of Picking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">Tea</a>&quot;, a folk song of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangxi">Jiangxi</a> belonging to the wider tradition of tea-picking operas.</p></div>
